            <div xml:id="d446">

                <pb facs="0742" n="616" xml:id="pg616"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/6680: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">MacMurray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1925-10-17T22:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 17,
                                1925—10 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received October 17—1:20
                        p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>451. Following from Shanghai: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“October 17, 1 p.m. Forces of Sun Chuan-fang have completely occupied
                            Shanghai without resistance, and advance guards are reported to have
                            reached outskirts of Soochow. It is reported that retreating Fengtien
                            soldiers have blown up one of the bridges near Soochow. Since there are
                            no other troops in this vicinity to oppose Sun no fighting is expected
                            here. Jacobs.”</p></quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">MacMurray</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
